#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 5210..6506
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/5
msgid ""
"One theory states she was the mother of the god\n"
"known as Quetzalcoatl.\n"
msgstr ""
"有一种说法称她是神明\n"
"魁札尔科亚特尔之母。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 6575..6993
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/6
msgid ""
"Quetzalcoatl...\n"
msgstr ""
"羽蛇神……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 7035..8400
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/7
msgid ""
"The quetzal is said to be an incarnation of\n"
"Quetzalcoatl, hence its name.\n"
msgstr ""
"凤尾绿咬鹃据说是羽蛇神的化身，\n"
"因此得名。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 8442..10309
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/8
msgid ""
"I get it. Well, this place definitely matches the\n"
"atmosphere of a cloud forest.\n"
msgstr ""
"明白了。这地方确实符合\n"
"云雾林的气氛。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 10323..11535
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/9
msgid ""
"Now, it may have seen better days, but that is still\n"
"a temple.\n"
msgstr ""
"虽说它已不复往昔，但那仍是\n"
"一座神庙。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 11591..12399
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/10
msgid ""
"So, be sure to show respect when you're inside.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以进去后务必表示敬意。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 12427..12901
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/11
msgid ""
"If the mood strikes me.\n"
msgstr ""
"看我心情。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 12956..14001
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/12
msgid ""
"Hmph! Well, you've got no one to blame but yourself\n"
msgstr ""
"哼！那要是索奇克察尔惩罚你，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 14043..14698
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/13
msgid ""
"if Xochiquetzal strikes you down.\n"
msgstr ""
"你也只能怪自己。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 445..1434
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/0
msgid ""
"I do not know if I recall such large ruins being\n"
"there...\n"
msgstr ""
"我不记得那里有\n"
"如此庞大的遗迹……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 1630..2897
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/1
msgid ""
"Well, didn't you say there's a lot we don't know\n"
"about Costa Rica's ancient civilizations?\n"
msgstr ""
"你不是说哥斯达黎加的古文明\n"
"还有很多未知吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 2925..4193
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/2
msgid ""
"You talked about some giant stone balls, too. What\n"
"are those?\n"
msgstr ""
"你也提到过一些巨大的石球。那些\n"
"是什么？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 4235..5154
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/3
msgid ""
"Oh, the Stone Spheres of Costa Rica?\n"
msgstr ""
"哦，哥斯达黎加石球？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 5266..6074
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/4
msgid ""
"They're an assortment of giant spheres carved\n"
"from stone\n"
msgstr ""
"它们是一批石雕的巨大球体，\n"
"种类繁多\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 6074..7383
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/5
msgid ""
"that were discovered in the jungles of Costa Rica\n"
"about 50 years ago.\n"
msgstr ""
"大约50年前在哥斯达黎加的丛林中被\n"
"发现。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 7411..7941
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/6
msgid ""
"What's so special about that?\n"
msgstr ""
"那有什么特别的？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 7983..9041
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/7
msgid ""
"What if I told you some of them are nearly perfect\n"
"spheres?\n"
msgstr ""
"如果我告诉你其中一些几乎是完美\n"
"球体呢？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 9167..10407
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/8
msgid ""
"And that they were carved out of granite, which is\n"
"quite a hard substance.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且它们由花岗岩雕成，这是一种\n"
"相当坚硬的物质。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 10448..11493
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/9
msgid ""
"Hmm, could be good for laying a trap.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯，用来设陷阱不错。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 11605..12483
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/10
msgid ""
"And if they're spherical, they'd roll easily, too...\n"
msgstr ""
"球形的还容易滚动……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 12496..12845
#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice 
#. timeline 1017..1281
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/11
#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/4
#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/8
#: codec/2/903/0x3879e0/1
#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/0
#: codec/2/909/0x38db70/0
#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/0
#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/0
#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/14
msgid ""
"Snake...\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0250_000_0
#. timeline 445..1365
#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/0
msgid ""
"So tell me, what do they mine around here?\n"
msgstr ""
"那这附近采什么矿？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0250_000_0
#. timeline 1393..1936
#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/1
msgid ""
"Gold, if I am not mistaken.\n"
msgstr ""
"没记错，是金矿。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0250_000_0
#. timeline 1978..3733
#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/2
msgid ""
"Gold?! No kidding. I wonder what'd be the fastest\n"
"way to...\n"
msgstr ""
"黄金？！没开玩笑吧。我想知道最快的\n"
"办法是什么……\n"

#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/3
msgid ""
"I do not know how much success they've had.\n"
msgstr ""
"不知道他们收益如何。\n"

#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/4
msgid ""
"You do not hear of anyone still operating mines\n"
"around here.\n"
msgstr ""
"你没听说这附近还有人仍在经营\n"
"矿场。\n"

#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/6
msgid ""
"Generally speaking, people here are not too thrilled\n"
"with outside capital\n"
msgstr ""
"一般来说，这里的人对外来资本\n"
"并不太欢迎\n"

#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/7
msgid ""
"coming in and taking away the country's natural\n"
"resources.\n"
msgstr ""
"进来并拿走这个国家的自然\n"
"资源。\n"

#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/8
msgid ""
"Four years ago, a group of protestors hurled\n"
"stones at the parliament building\n"
msgstr ""
"四年前，一群抗议者向\n"
"议会大楼投掷石块\n"

#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/9
msgid ""
"when people found out the country had been\n"
"bestowing mining rights to foreign companies.\n"
msgstr ""
"当人们发现这个国家一直在\n"
"将采矿权授予外国公司时。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 445..1783
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/0
msgid ""
"They must have had to clear a considerable\n"
"amount of forest to open up that mine.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们肯定不得不清理相当\n"
"数量的森林来开辟那座矿场。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 2020..3092
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/1
msgid ""
"No doubt. So much for any hiding places, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。藏身之处也没了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 3120..4207
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/2
msgid ""
"And it is not just the forest. Without the proper\n"
"precautions,\n"
msgstr ""
"而且不仅是森林。如果没有适当\n"
"预防措施，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 4277..5113
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/3
msgid ""
"the mine's waste water could pollute the\n"
"groundwater.\n"
msgstr ""
"矿场的废水可能会污染\n"
"地下水。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 5182..6339
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/4
msgid ""
"And to top it all off, they're developing nuclear\n"
"weapons there, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"最糟糕的是，他们还在那里开发核\n"
"武器。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 6450..7328
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/5
msgid ""
"How can people care so little about their own\n"
"country?\n"
msgstr ""
"人们怎么能对自己国家\n"
"如此漠不关心？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 7370..8038
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/6
msgid ""
"...I'm not the one to ask about that.\n"
msgstr ""
"……这问题别问我。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 8038..8930
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/7
msgid ""
"Well, you may have abandoned your country,\n"
msgstr ""
"你也许抛弃了自己的国家，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 9055..9752
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/8
msgid ""
"but you still treasure where you came from.\n"
msgstr ""
"但你依然珍视自己的故乡。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 10198..10504
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/9
#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/10
#: codec/2/914/0x392460/23
msgid ""
"You think so?\n"
msgstr ""
"是吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 10518..11312
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/10
msgid ""
"Sure. I know you do.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然。我知道你是这样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 11424..13931
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/11
msgid ""
"Paz, you... I... Whatever you do, never stop loving\n"
"your country.\n"
msgstr ""
"帕兹，你……我……无论你做什么，永远不要停止热爱\n"
"your country。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/0
msgid ""
"Since it was founded, my country has not once\n"
"been able to choose its own path.\n"
msgstr ""
"自建国以来，我的国家从未\n"
"能够选择自己的道路。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/1
msgid ""
"First Spain, then America. Over one hundred years\n"
"of this...\n"
msgstr ""
"先是西班牙，然后是美洲。一百多年来\n"
"都是如此……\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/2
#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/11
msgid ""
"I know.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/3
msgid ""
"In the 19th century,\n"
msgstr ""
"19世纪，\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/4
msgid ""
"an American mercenary named William Walker\n"
"seized power in Nicaragua.\n"
msgstr ""
"一位名叫威廉·沃克的美国雇佣兵\n"
"夺取了尼加拉瓜的政权。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/5
msgid ""
"I'd heard he exploited rivalries between the political\n"
"parties.\n"
msgstr ""
"我听说他利用了政党之间的\n"
"敌对关系。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/6
msgid ""
"Even after we expelled him,\n"
msgstr ""
"即便我们赶走他，\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/7
msgid ""
"the Americans sent in their Marines under the\n"
"pretext of quelling political unrest.\n"
msgstr ""
"美国人以平息政治动乱为\n"
"借口，派出了他们的海军陆战队。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/8
msgid ""
"And the real reason?\n"
msgstr ""
"真正原因？\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/9
msgid ""
"To intimidate the government and thwart the\n"
"construction of the Nicaragua Canal.\n"
msgstr ""
"为了恐吓政府并阻挠\n"
"尼加拉瓜运河的建设。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0880/0
msgid ""
"I thought the U.S. already has the rights to build a\n"
"canal in Nicaragua...\n"
msgstr ""
"我以为美国已经拥有在尼加拉瓜\n"
"修建运河的权利……\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0880/1
msgid ""
"They never intended to build a canal there. They\n"
"had already started digging in Panama.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们从未打算在那里修建运河。他们\n"
"已经在巴拿马开始挖掘了。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0880/2
msgid ""
"A canal in Nicaragua would break up the Panama\n"
"Canal's monopoly,\n"
msgstr ""
"尼加拉瓜的运河会打破巴拿马\n"
"运河的垄断，\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0880/3
msgid ""
"reason enough for America to stick its nose into\n"
"our affairs.\n"
msgstr ""
"这足以让美国插手\n"
"我们的事务。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0880/4
msgid ""
"They snagged the rights so nobody else could\n"
"build there...\n"
msgstr ""
"他们抢了权利，别人就没法\n"
"在那修建……\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0880/5
msgid ""
"It was General Sandino who finally stood up to los\n"
"yanquis.\n"
msgstr ""
"是桑地诺将军最终挺身对抗\n"
"美国佬。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/0
msgid ""
"General Sandino waged a guerrilla war against the\n"
"Marines,\n"
msgstr ""
"桑地诺将军对海军陆战队\n"
"发动了游击战，\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/1
msgid ""
"at last driving them out. He was a true hero, and -\n"
"to us Sandinistas - like a father.\n"
msgstr ""
"最终赶走了他们。他是真英雄，\n"
"对我们桑地诺人，就像父亲。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/2
msgid ""
"But when they pulled out, the Americans left us\n"
"something to remember them by.\n"
msgstr ""
"但他们撤走时，美国人留给我们\n"
"一样东西作纪念。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/3
msgid ""
"The National Guard.\n"
msgstr ""
"国民警卫队。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/4
msgid ""
"Yes, la Guardia. In name, a peacekeeping force.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错，国民警卫队。名义上是维和部队。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/5
msgid ""
"But in reality, Commander Somoza's personal army,\n"
"answering to no one else.\n"
msgstr ""
"实际上是索摩查司令的私人军队，\n"
"只听命于他一人。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/6
msgid ""
"Unable to stay silent, General Sandino went to\n"
"protest...\n"
msgstr ""
"桑地诺将军无法保持沉默，前去\n"
"抗议……\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/7
msgid ""
"and was assassinated by Somoza as he made his\n"
"way home.\n"
msgstr ""
"并在回家的路上\n"
"被索摩查暗杀。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/8
msgid ""
"It was then that Somoza and los sapos\n"
msgstr ""
"就在那时，索摩查和蟾蜍\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/9
msgid ""
"began to eat our country alive, from the inside.\n"
msgstr ""
"开始从内部活活吞噬我们的国家。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0f10/0
msgid ""
"It has been 40 years since the Somoza family\n"
"became the rulers of Nicaragua.\n"
msgstr ""
"索摩查家族统治尼加拉瓜，\n"
"已经四十年了。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/0
msgid ""
"The first Somoza was originally no more than the\n"
"commander of la Guardia.\n"
msgstr ""
"第一代索摩查原本不过是\n"
"国民警卫队的司令。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/1
msgid ""
"Ordinarily, a man of his station could never hope to\n"
"become president.\n"
msgstr ""
"按常理，以他的身份绝无可能\n"
"当上总统。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/2
msgid ""
"But the president at the time had no power to\n"
"back him.\n"
msgstr ""
"但当时的总统无力\n"
"支持他。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/3
msgid ""
"The only one with the strength to oppose him was\n"
"General Sandino.\n"
msgstr ""
"唯一有力量反对他的，只有\n"
"桑地诺将军。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/4
msgid ""
"....No. Better to say the General was the only one\n"
"who dared oppose him.\n"
msgstr ""
"……不。不如说，将军是唯一\n"
"敢于反对他的人。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/5
msgid ""
"There was nothing special about him.\n"
msgstr ""
"他并没有什么特别之处。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/6
msgid ""
"Above all, it takes a strong will to see justice done.\n"
"That is what he taught us.\n"
msgstr ""
"关键是，伸张正义需坚强意志。\n"
"这是他教我们的。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/7
msgid ""
"It's also what motivated Somoza to have him killed...\n"
msgstr ""
"也正是这一点促使索摩查杀了他……\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/8
msgid ""
"Yes. The rest was easy. He got rid of the\n"
"president, taking office in a sham election.\n"
msgstr ""
"是的。剩下的就简单了。他除掉了\n"
"总统，靠一场假选举上台。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/9
msgid ""
"And once he had power, he never gave it up.\n"
msgstr ""
"一旦掌权，他就再也没放手。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/10
msgid ""
"Talk about heavy-handed.\n"
msgstr ""
"真是够强硬的。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/11
msgid ""
"He had the Americans backing him, that's why.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是因为有美国人给他撑腰。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/12
msgid ""
"They didn't want to hand over power to a\n"
"rebellious general.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们不想把权力交给一个\n"
"叛逆的将军。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/13
msgid ""
"Even so, it's hard to believe Washington would give\n"
"its blessing to a guy like that.\n"
msgstr ""
"即便如此，也很难相信华盛顿会\n"
"祝福那种家伙。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/14
msgid ""
"The American President at the time put it this way:\n"
msgstr ""
"当时的美国总统是这么说的：\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/15
msgid ""
"\"Somoza may be a son of a bitch, but he's our son\n"
"of a bitch.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"“索摩查也许是个狗娘养的，但他是\n"
"咱们的狗娘养的。”\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/16
msgid ""
"In other words, better a dog or los sapos (Somoza\n"
"and counter-revolutionaries)\n"
msgstr ""
"换句话说，宁可要条狗或蟾蜍（索摩查\n"
"和反革命分子）\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/17
msgid ""
"than an anti-US regime.\n"
msgstr ""
"比反美政权更甚。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc1d60/0
msgid ""
"The Managua Earthquake struck two years ago,\n"
"the day before Christmas Eve.\n"
msgstr ""
"两年前的马那瓜大地震，\n"
"发生在平安夜的前一天。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc1d60/1
msgid ""
"Giant cracks opened up in the streets.\n"
msgstr ""
"街道裂开了巨大的缝隙。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc1d60/2
msgid ""
"Sleeping children were crushed in collapsing\n"
"houses.\n"
msgstr ""
"熟睡的孩子被压在\n"
"倒塌的房屋下。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc1d60/3
msgid ""
"No chance to escape. No visit from Santa Claus.\n"
msgstr ""
"无处可逃，也没有圣诞老人到来。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc1d60/4
msgid ""
"Thanks to Somoza, the old houses could not even\n"
"get rebuilt... It was a nightmare.\n"
msgstr ""
"因为索摩查，旧房连重建都做不到……\n"
"那是一场噩梦。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc1d60/5
msgid ""
"I heard the epicenter was right in the middle of the\n"
"city.\n"
msgstr ""
"听说震中\n"
"就在市区正中。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc1d60/6
msgid ""
"Even today, it's too dangerous to build on top of\n"
"the fault line.\n"
msgstr ""
"直到今天，断层线上\n"
"仍然危险到无法盖房。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc1d60/7
msgid ""
"The city center is still in ruins.\n"
msgstr ""
"市中心至今还是废墟。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc1d60/8
msgid ""
"And to make things worse, Somoza stole the\n"
"recovery money.\n"
msgstr ""
"更糟的是，索摩查\n"
"还贪污了救灾款。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc1d60/9
msgid ""
"We must not fail. We owe it to those who lost their\n"
"lives.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们不能失败。\n"
"要对得起那些逝去的人。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/0
msgid ""
"The river that flows between Nicaragua and Costa\n"
"Rica is el Río San Juan.\n"
msgstr ""
"流经尼加拉瓜和哥斯\n"
"黎巴嫩之间的河流是圣胡安河。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/1
msgid ""
"It connects Lago Cocibolca to el Mar Caribe.\n"
msgstr ""
"它连接科西博尔卡湖与加勒比海。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/2
msgid ""
"It is a gentle river, safe even for small boats. You\n"
"have to watch out for the sharks, though.\n"
msgstr ""
"这是一条平缓的河流，连小船也能安全通行。不过\n"
"你得小心鲨鱼。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/3
msgid ""
"Sharks? In a river?\n"
msgstr ""
"鲨鱼？在河？\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/4
msgid ""
"El tiburón toro live in the river. But there's nothing\n"
"to fear. San Juan will protect you always.\n"
msgstr ""
"公牛鲨生活在河里。但没什么\n"
"好怕的。圣胡安会永远保护你。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/5
msgid ""
"Juan?\n"
msgstr ""
"胡安？\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/6
msgid ""
"The Rio San Juan takes its name from San Juan,\n"
"the man who baptized Jesús.\n"
msgstr ""
"圣胡安河得名于圣胡安，\n"
"就是为耶稣施洗的人。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/7
msgid ""
"The man you call John the Baptist in your country.\n"
msgstr ""
"在你们国家叫施洗约翰。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/8
msgid ""
"John, huh... I'll be careful anyway. I'd hate to drown\n"
"- end up a John Doe.\n"
msgstr ""
"约翰，嗯……我还是小心点。我可不想淹死\n"
"成无名氏。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/0
msgid ""
"There is a volcanic island in Lago Cocibolca called\n"
"Ometepe.\n"
msgstr ""
"科西博尔卡湖有座火山岛，名叫\n"
"奥梅特佩。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/1
msgid ""
"It's formed from two connected volcanoes, shaped\n"
"like a porongo (gourd).\n"
msgstr ""
"它由两座相连火山构成，形状\n"
"像葫芦（porongo）。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/2
msgid ""
"The one with smoke coming out of it?\n"
msgstr ""
"就是那座冒烟的？\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/3
msgid ""
"That's the one. The smoking volcano is\n"
"Concepción. It erupts once in a while.\n"
msgstr ""
"就是那座。冒烟的火山是\n"
"康塞普西翁。它偶尔喷发。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/4
msgid ""
"The other one is Maderas.\n"
msgstr ""
"另一座是马德拉斯。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/5
msgid ""
"It's never erupted in recorded history. There's a\n"
"lake in the caldera at the top.\n"
msgstr ""
"有历史记录以来它从未喷发过。山顶的\n"
"火山口里有一个湖。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/6
msgid ""
"A crater lake... Let's hope there's not another\n"
"underground factory inside...\n"
msgstr ""
"火山口湖……希望里面没有另一个\n"
"地下工厂……\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/7
msgid ""
"Don't say that!\n"
msgstr ""
"别这么说！\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/8
msgid ""
"If Peace Walker's nukes detonated there, it would\n"
"destabilize the magma underneath.\n"
msgstr ""
"如果和平行者号的核弹在那里引爆，会\n"
"破坏下方岩浆的稳定。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/9
msgid ""
"It could cause the volcano to erupt again.\n"
msgstr ""
"可能导致火山再次喷发。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/10
msgid ""
"If that happens, my country is doomed. Snake, you\n"
"must stop Peace Walker!\n"
msgstr ""
"那样我国就完了。斯内克，你\n"
"必须阻止和平行者！\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/0
msgid ""
"We are Sandinistas, the heirs of General Sandino's\n"
"will.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们是桑地诺人，继承桑地诺将军\n"
"遗志。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/1
msgid ""
"Sandino... the father of modern guerrilla warfare.\n"
msgstr ""
"桑地诺……现代游击战之父。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/2
msgid ""
"To you, maybe. To us, he's more like a real father.\n"
msgstr ""
"对你或许。对我们，他更像真父亲。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/3
msgid ""
"That why you named yourselves after him?\n"
msgstr ""
"所以你们以他命名？\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/4
msgid ""
"Of course. La Frente Sandinista de Liberación\n"
"Nacional...\n"
msgstr ""
"当然。桑地诺民族解放\n"
"阵线……\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/5
msgid ""
"the Sandinista National Liberation Front is named\n"
"in his honor.\n"
msgstr ""
"桑地诺民族解放阵线以\n"
"他命名，以示纪念。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/6
msgid ""
"We share the General's goal - to take back our\n"
"country's freedom.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们和将军目标一致，夺回我们\n"
"国家的自由。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/7
msgid ""
"In his day, from America. In ours, from the despot\n"
"Somoza.\n"
msgstr ""
"他那时，敌人来自美国。我们这时，敌人是暴君\n"
"索摩查。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/8
msgid ""
"Times have changed, but the song remains the\n"
"same.\n"
msgstr ""
"时代变了，但歌还是那首\n"
"歌。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/9
msgid ""
"\"Patria Libre o Morir\"... That is our slogan.\n"
msgstr ""
"“自由祖国或死亡”……这是我们的口号。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/10
msgid ""
"El Che used to say the same thing, you know?\n"
msgstr ""
"切也曾说过同样的话。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/11
msgid ""
"\"Patria o Muerte\"... the slogan of the Cuban\n"
"Revolution.\n"
msgstr ""
"“祖国或死亡”……古巴\n"
"革命的标语。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/12
msgid ""
"So you're fighting for a socialist revolution, too,\n"
"then?\n"
msgstr ""
"这么说你们也是在为社会主义革命而战，\n"
"是吗？\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/13
msgid ""
"No. It's not about ideology. We only want to live\n"
"normal lives.\n"
msgstr ""
"不。无关意识形态。我们只想\n"
"正常生活。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/14
msgid ""
"We are sick of living in a country where you can\n"
"be beaten for walking down the street.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们受够了生活在一个可能因为走在街上\n"
"就被殴打的国家。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/15
msgid ""
"Where you never know if your neighbor is snitching\n"
"on you.\n"
msgstr ""
"在那儿，你不知邻居会不会背后\n"
"告发你。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/16
msgid ""
"Our goal is to give back the country to its people.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们的目标是把国家还给人民。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/17
msgid ""
"Yeah. The Cuban Revolution started out like that,\n"
"too...\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊。古巴革命当初也这样开始，\n"
"也是……\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/18
msgid ""
"We are few in number, but we will win.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们人少，但会赢。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/19
msgid ""
"Victoria o muerte. For a revolutionary, there is no\n"
"other fate.\n"
msgstr ""
"胜利或死亡。对革命者来说，没有\n"
"别的命运。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/0
msgid ""
"Augusto César Sandino... general and hero of\n"
"Nicaragua.\n"
msgstr ""
"奥古斯托·塞萨尔·桑地诺……尼加拉瓜的\n"
"将军和英雄。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/1
msgid ""
"Fifty years ago, conflict broke out between the\n"
"political parties of Nicaragua.\n"
msgstr ""
"五十年前，尼加拉瓜各政党之间\n"
"爆发了冲突。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/2
msgid ""
"The U.S. Marines intervened in the name of\n"
"restoring order.\n"
msgstr ""
"美国海军陆战队以恢复秩序为名\n"
"干预。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/3
msgid ""
"The only one who refused to listen to their call for\n"
"reconciliation was General Sandino.\n"
msgstr ""
"唯一拒绝响应他们和解呼吁的人，\n"
"就是桑地诺将军。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/4
msgid ""
"One man against the Marines... That takes guts.\n"
msgstr ""
"一人对抗海军陆战队……真有种。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/5
msgid ""
"The General wasn't a professional soldier. Neither\n"
"were his compadres.\n"
msgstr ""
"将军不是职业军人。他的\n"
"兄弟们也不是。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/6
msgid ""
"And they certainly could not match the Marines'\n"
"equipment.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们当然无法匹敌海军陆战队的\n"
"装备。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/7
msgid ""
"But he used the land to his advantage, lurking in\n"
"the fields and hills of Nicaragua,\n"
msgstr ""
"但他利用地形优势，潜伏在\n"
"尼加拉瓜的田野和山丘之中，\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/8
msgid ""
"and using surprise attacks to harass the Marines.\n"
msgstr ""
"用突袭骚扰海军陆战队。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/9
msgid ""
"I know. I've read plenty of textbooks on guerrilla\n"
"warfare.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道。我读过不少关于游击战的\n"
"教科书。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/10
msgid ""
"In the end, he drove them out. He was truly a role\n"
"model for us.\n"
msgstr ""
"最终，他赶走了他们。他真是我们的\n"
"榜样。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/11
msgid ""
"Yeah, but that was the '30s - didn't the Depression\n"
"have something to do with it?\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，但那是30年代——大萧条\n"
"跟这没关系吗？\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/12
msgid ""
"It takes cash to wage war.\n"
msgstr ""
"打仗得花钱。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/13
msgid ""
"Perhaps. But there is no denying what the General\n"
"accomplished.\n"
msgstr ""
"也许吧。但将军的成就\n"
"无可否认。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/14
msgid ""
"The people hailed him as the \"General de Hombres\n"
"Libres\" - the general of free men.\n"
msgstr ""
"人民称他为“自由人将军”\n"
"——General de Hombres Libres。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/15
msgid ""
"They loved him. And then...\n"
msgstr ""
"他们爱戴他。然后……\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/16
msgid ""
"He was assassinated - by Anastasio Somoza\n"
"Garcia, commander of la Guardia.\n"
msgstr ""
"他被暗杀了——凶手是安纳斯塔西奥·索摩查·\n"
"加西亚，国民警卫队司令。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/17
msgid ""
"The father of the current Somoza.\n"
msgstr ""
"现任索摩查的父亲。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/18
msgid ""
"Somoza had the Americans' backing. That is the\n"
"way things were.\n"
msgstr ""
"索摩查有美国人的支持。事情\n"
"就是这样。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/19
msgid ""
"The General may be dead, and the times may have\n"
"changed,\n"
msgstr ""
"将军可能已经死了，时代可能已经\n"
"变了，\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/20
msgid ""
"but his will lives on inside each of us.\n"
msgstr ""
"但他意志活在我们每人心中。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/21
msgid ""
"We are the sons and daughters of General Sandino.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们是桑地诺将军的儿女。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/0
msgid ""
"Hey. How's the watermelon business these days?\n"
msgstr ""
"嘿，最近西瓜生意怎么样？\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/1
msgid ""
"Not bad. I hear the compas back home are hanging\n"
"in there, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"不错。我听说家乡的同志们也\n"
"在坚持。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/2
msgid ""
"Good to hear.\n"
msgstr ""
"那就好。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/3
msgid ""
"...You know our nickname. I'm impressed.\n"
msgstr ""
"……你竟知我们绰号，佩服。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/4
msgid ""
"No wonder they call you Boss.\n"
msgstr ""
"难怪人家叫你BOSS。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/5
msgid ""
"You used to hide your weapons in hollowed-out\n"
"watermelons,\n"
msgstr ""
"你们以前把武器藏在挖空的\n"
"西瓜里，\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/6
msgid ""
"smuggle 'em right past the National Guard.\n"
msgstr ""
"就这么混过国民警卫队。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/7
msgid ""
"You even transported pineapple grenades that\n"
"way.\n"
msgstr ""
"你们甚至那样\n"
"运菠萝手榴弹。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/8
msgid ""
"The name caught on among sympathizers in the\n"
"region and...\n"
msgstr ""
"这名字在地区同情者中\n"
"传开，而且……\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/9
#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/39
#: codec/2/914/0x392460/18
msgid ""
"What are you talking about?\n"
msgstr ""
"你在说什么？\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/11
msgid ""
"They call us watermelon sellers because the\n"
"General's name\n"
msgstr ""
"他们叫我们西瓜贩子，因为\n"
"将军的名字\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/12
msgid ""
"sounds like the word for watermelon, sandía.\n"
msgstr ""
"听起来像西瓜，sandía。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/13
#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/9
msgid ""
"...Really?\n"
msgstr ""
"…真？\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/14
msgid ""
"Si.\n"
msgstr ""
"是。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/15
msgid ""
"Dammit, Kaz...\n"
msgstr ""
"可恶，卡兹…\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/0
msgid ""
"A revolution to bring peace to your country, huh.\n"
msgstr ""
"为祖国带来和平的革命，是吗。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/1
msgid ""
"No matter how much we fight, peace never gets\n"
"any closer, does it?\n"
msgstr ""
"无论怎么战斗，\n"
"和平都没有更近一步。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/2
msgid ""
"I do not like it, but it is the only way.\n"
msgstr ""
"我也不喜欢，但别无他法。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/3
msgid ""
"If we do not fight back, they'll just keep exploiting\n"
"us.\n"
msgstr ""
"不反抗，他们就\n"
"会一直压榨我们。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/4
msgid ""
"You want proof? Look at our country's history.\n"
msgstr ""
"要证据？看看我国的历史。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/5
msgid ""
"Revolution is a means and not an end, I know.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道，革命是手段而非目的。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/6
msgid ""
"When the revolution is victorious, I want my\n"
"country to be at peace.\n"
msgstr ""
"革命胜利后，\n"
"我希望祖国能享有和平。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/7
msgid ""
"But to bring peace, we have to first eliminate that\n"
"traitorous scum.\n"
msgstr ""
"但要实现和平，\n"
"就得先除掉那个叛徒败类。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/8
msgid ""
"It's an old saying: \"We make war that we may live\n"
"in peace.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"有句老话：「我们发动战争，\n"
"是为了能生活在和平中。」\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/9
msgid ""
"Who said it?\n"
msgstr ""
"谁说的？\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/10
msgid ""
"Aristotle.\n"
msgstr ""
"亚里士多德。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/11
msgid ""
"You know your history.\n"
msgstr ""
"你很懂历史。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/12
msgid ""
"I had a good teacher.\n"
msgstr ""
"我有个好老师。\n"

#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/0
msgid ""
"I noticed you call Che Guevara \"El Che.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"你管切·格瓦拉叫“El Che”。\n"

#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/1
msgid ""
"Not just us. Everyone in these parts does.\n"
msgstr ""
"不只我们。这的人都这么叫。\n"

#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/2
msgid ""
"\"Che\" was always his nickname. It does not feel\n"
"right to call him by his last name.\n"
msgstr ""
"“切”一直是他的昵称。叫他\n"
"姓，感觉不对。\n"

#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/3
msgid ""
"...I was shocked the first time I saw you. You look\n"
"so much like him.\n"
msgstr ""
"…我第一次见你时很震惊。你太像\n"
"他了。\n"

#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/4
msgid ""
"I look like \"El Che\", huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"我像“El Che”？\n"

#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/5
msgid ""
"Sort of. Not in the face. It's more... the way you\n"
"carry yourself...\n"
msgstr ""
"有点像。不是脸。更像是…你的\n"
"举手投足…\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 7397..8136
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/6
msgid ""
"I guess Che's a hero to the Sandinistas, too?\n"
msgstr ""
"切对桑地诺派来说也是英雄吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 8164..10156
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/7
msgid ""
"Of course. The FSLN was formed in the spirit of\n"
"the ideologies championed by El Che and Fidel.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然。FSLN正是本着El Che和\n"
"菲德尔所倡导的思想成立的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 10421..12775
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/8
msgid ""
"Fidel... Fidel Castro. So you're trying to bring the\n"
"Cuban Revolution to Nicaragua.\n"
msgstr ""
"菲德尔…卡斯特罗。你们想把\n"
"古巴革命带到尼加拉瓜。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 12845..14642
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/9
msgid ""
"Well, we were. But Cuba isn't what it once was...\n"
"Not since El Che left.\n"
msgstr ""
"曾经是。但古巴已不复当年…\n"
"自El Che走后。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 14740..16314
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/10
msgid ""
"El Che was a true revolutionary. He fought - and\n"
"died - for the people.\n"
msgstr ""
"El Che是真正的革命者。他为人民\n"
"战斗——并牺牲。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 16370..17387
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/11
msgid ""
"He worked harder than anybody, and he was a\n"
"righteous man.\n"
msgstr ""
"他比谁都努力，他是个\n"
"正直的人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 17442..19045
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/12
msgid ""
"Even as a minister of Cuba, he gave up his\n"
"weekends to work on the farms and public works.\n"
msgstr ""
"即使身为古巴部长，他也放弃周末\n"
"去农场和公共工程干活。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 19100..19560
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/13
msgid ""
"As a volunteer, no less.\n"
msgstr ""
"还是当志愿者。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 19644..20271
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/14
msgid ""
"Yeah, I've heard the stories.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，故事我听过。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 20326..21441
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/15
msgid ""
"But when you think about it, wasn't it that\n"
"obsession that did him in?\n"
msgstr ""
"但想想看，不正是那份\n"
"执念害了他吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 21483..21831
#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 2048..2326
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/16
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/1
msgid ""
"How do you mean?\n"
msgstr ""
"什么意思？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 21887..23517
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/17
msgid ""
"We can't all be supermen. He thought the ideals he\n"
"applied in Cuba would work in Bolivia.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们不可能都是超人。他以为古巴\n"
"行得通的理想，玻利维亚也行。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 23558..25077
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/18
msgid ""
"But, he failed to win converts and the support of\n"
"the peasants, and it cost him his life.\n"
msgstr ""
"但他没能争取到皈依者和\n"
"农民的支持，为此丢了命。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 25175..25927
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/19
msgid ""
"Maybe... maybe you're right.\n"
msgstr ""
"也许…你说得对。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 26010..27278
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/20
msgid ""
"But at least he did not steal from those peasants,\n"
"no matter how hard things got.\n"
msgstr ""
"但至少他没偷农民的东西，\n"
"再难也没偷。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 27320..27473
#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 1309..1476
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/21
#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/14
#: codec/1/206/0xce040/7
#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/2
#: codec/1/246/0xf6dc0/2
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/1
#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/12
#: codec/2/913/0x391bb0/1
msgid ""
"Yeah.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 27515..28017
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/22
msgid ""
"I can sympathize with that.\n"
msgstr ""
"我能理解。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 28100..29312
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/23
msgid ""
"There's plenty of guerrillas out there who'd rob\n"
"their own people to feed their revolutions.\n"
msgstr ""
"游击队里多的是抢自己人\n"
"喂革命的人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 29354..31249
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/24
msgid ""
"If we had a comandante like him, the Sandinistas\n"
"would find the will to fight.\n"
msgstr ""
"若有个像他的指挥官，桑地诺\n"
"就有斗志了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 501..1407
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/0
msgid ""
"You called that giant chopper an \"hombre nuevo\"...\n"
msgstr ""
"你把那架大直升机叫\"hombre nuevo\"……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 1407..2201
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/1
msgid ""
"Si. It means \"new man.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"Si，意为\"新人\"。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 2229..2563
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/2
msgid ""
"\"New man\"?\n"
msgstr ""
"\"新人\"？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 2605..3789
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/3
msgid ""
"There was nobody piloting that thing. It must be\n"
"controlled by machine.\n"
msgstr ""
"那东西根本没人驾驶。肯定是由机器\n"
"控制的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 3817..5391
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/4
msgid ""
"Yeah, it seems that way. No human being could pull\n"
"off those crazy maneuvers.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，看来如此。没人能做出\n"
"那些疯狂动作。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 5433..6561
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/5
msgid ""
"But it's not crazy - it's smart. It sings, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"那不叫疯，叫聪明。它还会唱歌。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 6603..8038
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/6
msgid ""
"When we first saw it, one of my men said, \"Pilot\n"
"must be an hombre nuevo.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"初见时，我手下说：“飞行员\n"
"准是新人。”\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 8080..8721
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/7
msgid ""
"Me, I do not like the name.\n"
msgstr ""
"我嘛，不喜欢这名字。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 8735..8986
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/8
#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/2
msgid ""
"Why?\n"
msgstr ""
"为什么？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 9000..10017
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/9
msgid ""
"\"Hombre nuevo\" was what El Che was striving to\n"
"become.\n"
msgstr ""
"“新人”正是切·格瓦拉想\n"
"成为的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 10058..57662
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/10
msgid ""
"What all of us who joined the Sandinistas strive to\n"
"become. That's why!\n"
msgstr ""
"我们加入桑地诺的人都想\n"
"成为那样。就是这样！\n"

#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/11
msgid ""
"An hombre nuevo is one who finds joy in virtue\n"
"and voluntary labor...\n"
msgstr ""
"新人就是在美德\n"
"和自愿劳动中找到快乐的人……\n"

#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/12
msgid ""
"It makes me furious to see the name given to such\n"
"a monster.\n"
msgstr ""
"这名字用在怪物身上，\n"
"让我怒火中烧。\n"

#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/13
msgid ""
"I'll bet.\n"
msgstr ""
"我信。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 459..1198
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/0
msgid ""
"Chico called that helicopter el colibri...\n"
msgstr ""
"奇科管那直升机叫el colibri……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 1253..2229
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/1
msgid ""
"Our name for the hummingbird. You saw how that\n"
"chopper moved...\n"
msgstr ""
"我们给蜂鸟起的名字。你看到那架\n"
"直升机是怎么动的了……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 2270..2856
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/2
msgid ""
"how it hovered in midair like a hummingbird.\n"
msgstr ""
"像蜂鸟一样悬停在空中。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 2911..3650
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/3
msgid ""
"Hell've a lot bigger than a bird, though.\n"
msgstr ""
"可它比鸟大太多了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 3691..4500
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/4
msgid ""
"True. But better than hombre nuevo, don't you\n"
"think?\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。但比“新人”更好，你不\n"
"觉得吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 4555..5419
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/5
msgid ""
"When you get kidnapped by el colibri, it's all over.\n"
msgstr ""
"被el colibri抓走，就完了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 5503..6673
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/6
msgid ""
"They take you to a prison camp, and torture you\n"
"until you snitch on your compas.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们会把你带到战俘营，折磨你\n"
"直到你出卖你的战友。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 6715..7202
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/7
msgid ""
"That's what took Chico...\n"
msgstr ""
"奇科就是这么被抓的……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 7244..8484
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/8
msgid ""
"They have no mercy. Once you've talked, they toss\n"
"you out like trash...\n"
msgstr ""
"他们毫不留情。你一开口，\n"
"就被当垃圾扔掉……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 8582..9459
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/9
msgid ""
"I knew this, and still I could not save Chico.\n"
msgstr ""
"我明知如此，却还是救不了奇科。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 9613..10616
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/10
msgid ""
"If he cannot be saved, I'll do what must be done...\n"
msgstr ""
"如果救不了他，我会做该做的事……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 10671..11187
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/11
msgid ""
"Don't write him off like that.\n"
msgstr ""
"别这么早就放弃他。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 11270..12538
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/12
msgid ""
"Sometimes you have to survive, even if it means\n"
"sacrificing your honor.\n"
msgstr ""
"有时你必须活下去，即使这意味着\n"
"牺牲你的荣誉。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 12594..13486
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/13
msgid ""
"I'll get him back. I promise.\n"
msgstr ""
"我会把他带回来。我保证。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/0
msgid ""
"Snake, I need your opinion. How strong are the\n"
"enemy's mercenaries?\n"
msgstr ""
"Snake，我需要你的看法。敌人的雇佣兵\n"
"有多强？\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/1
msgid ""
"They're well trained. They've got more than enough\n"
"men...\n"
msgstr ""
"他们训练有素，人手\n"
"绰绰有余……\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/2
msgid ""
"Seasoned, too - a lot of them probably saw action\n"
"in Vietnam. They're a tough bunch.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且老练，很多人可能在越南\n"
"打过仗。他们很难缠。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/3
msgid ""
"And armed to the teeth.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且全副武装。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/4
msgid ""
"I don't think I've ever seen a mercenary force field\n"
"that many tanks and attack choppers.\n"
msgstr ""
"我想我从没见过一支雇佣兵部队能部署\n"
"那么多坦克和攻击直升机。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/5
msgid ""
"It shows how much cash they have to throw\n"
"around.\n"
msgstr ""
"说明他们有多少钱可以随意\n"
"挥霍。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/6
msgid ""
"And connections - how did they get access to\n"
"such weapons?\n"
msgstr ""
"还有人脉，他们怎么弄到\n"
"这种武器的？\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/7
msgid ""
"How do you think? They're backed by the one and\n"
"only CIA.\n"
msgstr ""
"你说呢？背后正是\n"
"独一无二的CIA。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/8
msgid ""
"And here we are, half of us farmers and the other\n"
"half students. Children, even!\n"
msgstr ""
"而我们呢，一半是农民，另一半\n"
"是学生。甚至还有孩子！\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/9
msgid ""
"And weapons... We're so short on guns we have to\n"
"steal them from the enemy.\n"
msgstr ""
"还有武器……我们枪太少了，只能\n"
"从敌人那里偷。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/10
msgid ""
"As much as I hate to say it, we're always going to\n"
"be on the defensive.\n"
msgstr ""
"尽管我很不想这么说，但我们永远都会\n"
"处于守势。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/12
msgid ""
"And mi viejo... Without him, we...\n"
msgstr ""
"还有我老爹……没了他，我们……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice 
#. timeline 16258..16690
#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/13
#: codec/2/903/0x3879e0/15
msgid ""
"Yeah, I know.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯，我知道。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/14
msgid ""
"...I don't know if we can win.\n"
msgstr ""
"……不知能不能赢。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/15
msgid ""
"Can we, Snake?\n"
msgstr ""
"我们能赢吗，SNAKE？\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/16
msgid ""
"Stop feeling sorry for yourself.\n"
msgstr ""
"别自怨自艾了。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/17
#: codec/2/905/0x389770/4
#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/48
msgid ""
"But...\n"
msgstr ""
"可是……\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/18
msgid ""
"Amanda!\n"
msgstr ""
"阿曼达！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 4959..5099
#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 3761..3914
#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_myo_rad_0190_000_0
#. timeline 417..557
#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/19
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/3
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/3
#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/17
#: codec/1/255/0xff000/8
#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/21
#: codec/2/904/0x388570/13
#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/46
#: codec/2/914/0x392460/12
#: codec/2/919/0x3971e0/1
msgid ""
"What?\n"
msgstr ""
"什么？\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/20
msgid ""
"Listen to me. Don't ever let your men hear you talk\n"
"like that.\n"
msgstr ""
"听我说。别让手下听见你\n"
"说这种话。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/21
msgid ""
"...I...\n"
msgstr ""
"……我……\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/22
msgid ""
"You're their leader, and a leader has to stand tall.\n"
"Even when times get tough.\n"
msgstr ""
"你是他们的领袖，领袖必须挺直腰杆。\n"
"哪怕时局艰难。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/23
msgid ""
"When it feels like the fear and uncertainty could\n"
"crush you.\n"
msgstr ""
"当恐惧和不安仿佛\n"
"要把你压垮时。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/24
msgid ""
"You're the one your comrades look to for\n"
"reassurance. That's what a leader is. Don't forget it.\n"
msgstr ""
"战友们指望你来安心。\n"
"这就是领袖。别忘了。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/25
msgid ""
"...Snake...\n"
msgstr ""
"……SNAKE……\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/26
msgid ""
"If you're looking for comfort, go find a church.\n"
"That's all I've got to say.\n"
msgstr ""
"想找安慰，去教堂。\n"
"我就说这些。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/27
msgid ""
"You are right. I am sorry. I need to pull myself\n"
"together.\n"
msgstr ""
"你说得对。抱歉。我得\n"
"振作起来。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/28
msgid ""
"You'll be fine. I know you have it in you.\n"
msgstr ""
"你会没事，你有这本事。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5eb0/0
msgid ""
"Claymores are directional anti-personnel landmines.\n"
msgstr ""
"阔刀地雷是定向杀伤人员地雷。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5eb0/1
msgid ""
"Their blast radius is approximately 70 vara (60 yd),\n"
msgstr ""
"杀伤半径约70瓦拉（60码），\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5eb0/2
msgid ""
"sending over 700 metal fragments through the air\n"
"at a 60º angle.\n"
msgstr ""
"以60度角抛射出\n"
"700多枚金属破片。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5eb0/3
msgid ""
"But since they're directional, you can simply disarm\n"
"them from their blind side.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过因为它是定向的，\n"
"从背面就能直接拆除。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/0
msgid ""
"The land in our country belongs to us, and yet it\n"
"doesn't belong to us.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们国家的土地属于我们，\n"
"却又不属于我们。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/2
msgid ""
"Along the coast, it is all banana groves. And in the\n"
"mountains, it is coffee.\n"
msgstr ""
"沿海全是香蕉园。山里\n"
"则是咖啡。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/3
msgid ""
"I guess in that way it's not so different from here.\n"
msgstr ""
"这么说来跟这里也差不多。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/4
msgid ""
"Plantations...\n"
msgstr ""
"庄园……\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/5
msgid ""
"Almost all the bananas and coffee are sold as\n"
"exports.\n"
msgstr ""
"几乎全部香蕉和咖啡都\n"
"出口卖掉。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/6
msgid ""
"The landlords keep the money for themselves,\n"
"leaving precious little to the farmers.\n"
msgstr ""
"地主把钱据为己有，\n"
"只留给农民一丁点。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/7
msgid ""
"Worse, the biggest landowners in the country are\n"
"Somoza and his family.\n"
msgstr ""
"更糟的是，全国最大的地主\n"
"就是索摩查一家。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/8
msgid ""
"But it does bring in foreign currency...\n"
msgstr ""
"但至少能赚外汇……\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/9
msgid ""
"I doubt even that, at least for bananas. The\n"
"plantations are owned by American corporations.\n"
msgstr ""
"我看未必，至少香蕉不是。\n"
"种植园属于美国公司。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/10
msgid ""
"The bananas are processed in factories on the\n"
"plantations and exported to America from private\n"
"ports...\n"
msgstr ""
"香蕉在种植园里的工厂加工，\n"
"然后从私人港口出口到美国……\n"
"\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/11
msgid ""
"It's like having little American enclaves along the\n"
"coast of Nicaragua.\n"
msgstr ""
"就像尼加拉瓜沿海\n"
"散布着美国飞地。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/12
msgid ""
"But the farmers have no choice but to go work\n"
"there...\n"
msgstr ""
"可农民别无选择，只能\n"
"去那里干活……\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/13
msgid ""
"Es ridículo! The people have to take their land\n"
"back.\n"
msgstr ""
"太荒唐了！人民必须\n"
"夺回土地。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/14
msgid ""
"It is one of the things we're fighting for.\n"
msgstr ""
"这就是我们战斗的目标之一。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/0
msgid ""
"Tell me... when exactly did you realize your dad\n"
"was working with the KGB?\n"
msgstr ""
"告诉我……你究竟何时\n"
"发现你父亲在为克格勃做事？\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/1
msgid ""
"About six months ago. Up until then, we only had\n"
"beans to eat.\n"
msgstr ""
"大约半年前。在那之前，\n"
"我们只有豆子吃。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/2
msgid ""
"And then suddenly we started to get eggs and\n"
"flour. Our bullet shortage simply disappeared.\n"
msgstr ""
"后来突然有了蛋和面粉。\n"
"子弹短缺就这么没了。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/3
msgid ""
"How'd he get the cocaine?\n"
msgstr ""
"可卡因哪来的？\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/4
msgid ""
"Ask the KGB. All we did here was process it.\n"
msgstr ""
"问克格勃。我们只管加工。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/5
msgid ""
"Coca plants grow here, too,\n"
msgstr ""
"这里也种古柯，\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/6
msgid ""
"but to my knowledge almost all of the stuff we\n"
"used came from Colombia and Bolivia.\n"
msgstr ""
"但据我所知，用的料几乎都来自\n"
"哥伦比亚和玻利维亚。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/7
msgid ""
"It's processed in a factory and then shipped to\n"
"ports on the Caribbean Sea.\n"
msgstr ""
"在工厂加工后运往\n"
"加勒比海沿岸港口。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/8
msgid ""
"Where does it go after that?\n"
msgstr ""
"之后运去哪？\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/9
msgid ""
"I never thought about it.... I mean, I did not want to\n"
"think about it.\n"
msgstr ""
"我从未想过……我是说，我不想去\n"
"想这件事。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/10
msgid ""
"The biggest cocaine consumer in the world is the\n"
"United States.\n"
msgstr ""
"全球最大的可卡因消费国就是\n"
"美国。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/11
msgid ""
"I'm guessing they smuggle it in on vessels\n"
"disguised as fishing boats.\n"
msgstr ""
"我猜是用伪装成渔船的\n"
"船走私进去。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/12
msgid ""
"Wait. La CIA uses that route, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"等等。CIA也用这条线。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/13
msgid ""
"Are you telling me they're selling cocaine to their\n"
"own country?\n"
msgstr ""
"你是说他们往自己国家\n"
"卖可卡因？\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/14
msgid ""
"Looks that way.\n"
msgstr ""
"看来是。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/15
msgid ""
"Those bastards are turning their own children into\n"
"junkies? Are they insane?!\n"
msgstr ""
"那帮混蛋把自家孩子变成\n"
"瘾君子？疯了吗？！\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/16
msgid ""
"No, just afraid. Afraid of a communist Central\n"
"America.\n"
msgstr ""
"不，只是怕。怕中美洲\n"
"落入共产党手。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/0
msgid ""
"La CIA calls their new toy Peace Walker, eh?\n"
msgstr ""
"中情局把他们的新玩具叫和平行者？\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/1
msgid ""
"Yeah... So?\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊……怎么了？\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/2
msgid ""
"It is a insult to us Nicos.\n"
msgstr ""
"这对我们尼加拉瓜人是种侮辱。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/3
msgid ""
"Because of the guy you were talking about?\n"
"Walker?\n"
msgstr ""
"因为你们说的\n"
"那个人？沃克？\n"

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/0
msgid ""
"Amanda! When did you join up with the Sandinistas?\n"
msgstr ""
"阿曼达！你何时加入桑地诺派？\n"

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/1
msgid ""
"About a year ago, when I went into the mountains\n"
"with mi viejo and his group.\n"
msgstr ""
"大概一年前，我跟老爹\n"
"和他的人进了山。\n"

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/2
msgid ""
"I thought your dad was with the FSLN from the\n"
"start.\n"
msgstr ""
"我以为你爸一开始\n"
"就在FSLN。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 3719..5419
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/3
msgid ""
"No. He fought alongside General Sandino, but after\n"
"that he retired for a while.\n"
msgstr ""
"不。他跟桑地诺将军并肩作战，\n"
"之后退隐了一阵。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 5489..6617
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/4
msgid ""
"He found a job, got a wife and a house, and raised\n"
"us kids.\n"
msgstr ""
"他找了工作，娶妻买房，\n"
"把我们养大。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 6715..7453
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/5
msgid ""
"Then one day some Sandinista students came by...\n"
msgstr ""
"后来有天来了几个桑地诺学生……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 7481..8345
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/6
msgid ""
"And he felt the old fire in his belly?\n"
msgstr ""
"他又热血沸腾了？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 8373..9654
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/7
msgid ""
"Something like that. All he did was help them\n"
"escape from la Guardia, though.\n"
msgstr ""
"差不多。不过他只是帮他们\n"
"从国民警卫队手里逃走。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 9710..10295
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/8
msgid ""
"But then la Guardia showed up.\n"
msgstr ""
"可国民警卫队来了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 10407..11549
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/9
msgid ""
"They broke into our house and began pushing him\n"
"around, shouting questions.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们闯进我家，推搡他，\n"
"吼着逼问。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 11591..12301
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/10
msgid ""
"I'm guessing he kept his mouth shut.\n"
msgstr ""
"我猜他一个字都没说。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 12343..13681
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/11
msgid ""
"No matter how hard they hit him. Our house was\n"
"trashed.\n"
msgstr ""
"不管怎么打他。我们家被砸得\n"
"稀烂。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 13778..14935
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/12
msgid ""
"After that, he was on their list - they harassed him\n"
"day and night.\n"
msgstr ""
"之后他上了他们的名单，日夜\n"
"骚扰他。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 15032..15966
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/13
msgid ""
"It was only then that he gave himself over to the\n"
"Sandinistas.\n"
msgstr ""
"直到那时，他才投奔了\n"
"桑地诺派。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 16063..17010
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/14
msgid ""
"He kept it hidden from us at first, so we would not\n"
"get hurt.\n"
msgstr ""
"起初他瞒着我们，怕我们\n"
"受牵连。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 17387..17916
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/15
msgid ""
"He sounds like a good father.\n"
msgstr ""
"他像个好父亲。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 18000..19964
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/16
msgid ""
"He was... But my mother got fed up with it. She left\n"
"us. I don't blame her.\n"
msgstr ""
"他曾是……但我妈受够了。她离开\n"
"我们。我不怪她。\n"

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/17
msgid ""
"Why didn't you go with her?\n"
msgstr ""
"你为啥不跟她走？\n"

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/18
msgid ""
"It was a hard decision, for sure.\n"
msgstr ""
"这决定确实很难。\n"

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/19
msgid ""
"But like my father, I couldn't let Somoza get away\n"
"with his crimes. But most of all...\n"
msgstr ""
"但像我父亲一样，我不能让索摩查逍遥\n"
"法外。最重要的是……\n"

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/20
#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/0
msgid ""
"Chico.\n"
msgstr ""
"奇科。\n"

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/21
msgid ""
"...He is too much like his papá. One way or the\n"
"other he was going to stay.\n"
msgstr ""
"……他太像他爸了。无论如何他都\n"
"会留下。\n"

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/22
msgid ""
"And I could not leave him behind.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不能丢下他。\n"

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/23
msgid ""
"Soon enough la Guardia drove us out, and we\n"
"found ourselves in the mountains...\n"
msgstr ""
"很快国民警卫队就把我们赶了出去，我们\n"
"流落到山里……\n"

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/24
msgid ""
"It just kind of happened\n"
msgstr ""
"就这么发生了\n"

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/25
msgid ""
"For an accidental revolutionary, you sure put up a\n"
"hell of a fight.\n"
msgstr ""
"作为一个意外的革命者，你打得可真\n"
"够狠的。\n"

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/26
msgid ""
"The mountains make men into warriors. The\n"
"training is harsh,\n"
msgstr ""
"大山把人磨炼成战士。训练很\n"
"艰苦，\n"

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/27
msgid ""
"but it brings us that much closer to being hombres\n"
"nuevos.\n"
msgstr ""
"但这让我们更接近成为新\n"
"人类。\n"

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/28
msgid ""
"Chico couldn't ask for a better sister.\n"
msgstr ""
"奇科再找不到更好的姐姐。\n"

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/29
msgid ""
"I can see why they picked you to be comandante.\n"
msgstr ""
"我懂他们为啥选你当指挥官。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/0
msgid ""
"When I was little, I came down with malaria.\n"
msgstr ""
"我小时候得过疟疾。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/1
msgid ""
"Unlucky for me, it was the bad kind. I was in a\n"
"daze the whole time,\n"
msgstr ""
"倒霉的是，是最凶的那种。我一直\n"
"昏昏沉沉，\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/2
msgid ""
"and at one point they said I was not going to make\n"
"it.\n"
msgstr ""
"有一阵他们说我挺不过\n"
"去了。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/3
msgid ""
"Malarial encephalopathy. I hear it's pretty common\n"
"in tropical malaria cases.\n"
msgstr ""
"疟疾脑病。我听说热带疟疾里挺\n"
"常见的。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/4
msgid ""
"Even today, my memory sometimes gets a little\n"
"fuzzy.\n"
msgstr ""
"到今天，我记忆有时还会有点\n"
"模糊。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/5
msgid ""
"Since then I've had this fear of mosquitoes... When\n"
"I hear them buzzing nearby, I get jumpy.\n"
msgstr ""
"从那以后我就怕蚊子……每当\n"
"听到附近嗡嗡叫，我就心惊肉跳。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/6
msgid ""
"That explains the chain-smoking?\n"
msgstr ""
"所以你烟不离手？\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/7
msgid ""
"Si. I thought it might help keep the mosquitoes\n"
"away, just a little.\n"
msgstr ""
"是。我以为这能赶远点蚊子，\n"
"哪怕一点点。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/8
msgid ""
"Maybe it's all in my head. You're the same way,\n"
"right?\n"
msgstr ""
"也许是我心理作用。你也一样，\n"
"对吧？\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/9
msgid ""
"I will say this - I prefer a cigar over mosquitoes.\n"
msgstr ""
"我宁愿抽雪茄也不想见蚊子。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/10
msgid ""
"Me, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"我也是。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/11
msgid ""
"I've gotta hand it to you. It takes guts to conquer\n"
"your fear like that\n"
msgstr ""
"我服你。像那样克服\n"
"恐惧，需要很大勇气。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/12
msgid ""
"and live a guerrilla's life in the wild.\n"
msgstr ""
"在野外打游击，真需要胆量。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/13
msgid ""
"It is nothing. El Che did not let asthma stop him\n"
"from leading the revolution.\n"
msgstr ""
"这没什么。切·格瓦拉没有让哮喘阻止他\n"
"领导革命。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/14
msgid ""
"Compared to him, I am no hero.\n"
msgstr ""
"跟他比，我算不上英雄。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/0
msgid ""
"I'm sorry to hear about your dad.\n"
msgstr ""
"你爸的事，我很遗憾。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/1
msgid ""
"Thank you for saying that... Mi viejo was the leader\n"
"of the frente.\n"
msgstr ""
"谢谢你这么说……我老爹曾是\n"
"frente的领袖。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/2
msgid ""
"He was the last of the generation that knew\n"
"General Sandino...\n"
msgstr ""
"他是认识桑地诺将军那代人中\n"
"最后一位……\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/3
msgid ""
"He saw the General's exploits first-hand as a boy.\n"
msgstr ""
"他小时候亲眼见过将军的事迹。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/4
msgid ""
"He would tell us stories about it all the time... and\n"
"about how the General was assassinated.\n"
msgstr ""
"他总给我们讲那些故事……还有\n"
"将军是如何被暗杀的。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/5
msgid ""
"Did you know he was getting money from the KGB?\n"
msgstr ""
"你知道他从克格勃拿钱吗？\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/6
msgid ""
"I had some idea... But I did not have the courage to\n"
"confront him about it.\n"
msgstr ""
"我有些猜想……但我没有勇气\n"
"去当面问他。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/7
msgid ""
"I know it was a painful decision for him to make.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道那对他是个痛苦的决定。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/8
#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/9
msgid ""
"I can imagine.\n"
msgstr ""
"我能想象。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/9
msgid ""
"Yes, my father was a good man. I loved him as a\n"
"daughter. And his soldiers believed in him.\n"
msgstr ""
"是的，我父亲是好人。我像\n"
"女儿一样爱他。士兵们也信他。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/10
msgid ""
"Thanks to him, la Frente held together even in the\n"
"worst of times.\n"
msgstr ""
"多亏他，即使最艰难时，\n"
"la Frente也团结在一起。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/11
msgid ""
"I don't know if I can ever fill his shoes...\n"
msgstr ""
"不知我能否接他的班……\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/0
msgid ""
"Chico's 12, right?\n"
msgstr ""
"奇科12岁吧？\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/2
msgid ""
"Isn't he a little... short for his age?\n"
msgstr ""
"他比同龄人矮了点？\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/3
msgid ""
"...Malnourishment. Food is hard to come by when\n"
"you're running around in the jungle...\n"
msgstr ""
"……营养不良。当你在丛林里\n"
"四处奔波时，食物很难弄到……\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/4
msgid ""
"He's got quite an appetite.\n"
msgstr ""
"他胃口真大。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/5
msgid ""
"I know!\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道！\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/6
msgid ""
"I didn't want him to come in the first place.\n"
msgstr ""
"我本来就不想让他来。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/7
msgid ""
"But there was no one to take him in. I had no\n"
"choice but to look after him.\n"
msgstr ""
"但没人愿意收留他。我别无\n"
"选择，只能照顾他。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/8
msgid ""
"Don't be so hard on yourself.\n"
msgstr ""
"别太自责了。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/9
msgid ""
"Sometimes it's better for a kid to be with his family\n"
"than far away, in a safe place.\n"
msgstr ""
"有时候，孩子跟家人在一起\n"
"比远在安全的地方更好。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/10
msgid ""
"Thank you...\n"
msgstr ""
"谢谢……\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/11
msgid ""
"Promise me this, though. When your fight is over,\n"
"make sure he gets a proper education.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过，你要答应我。等你战斗结束，\n"
"一定让他接受正规教育。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/12
msgid ""
"Give him a chance to be something other than a\n"
"guerrilla.\n"
msgstr ""
"给他机会，让他不必只做\n"
"游击队员。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/13
msgid ""
"It's not too late to teach him something other than\n"
"fighting.\n"
msgstr ""
"现在教他点战斗以外的东西\n"
"还不算晚。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/14
msgid ""
"OK. I promise.\n"
msgstr ""
"好。我答应你。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/15
msgid ""
"...You know what book Chico really likes?\n"
msgstr ""
"……你知道奇科最爱什么书？\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/16
msgid ""
"The \"World Encyclopedia of Mysterious Creatures.\"\n"
"The Loch Ness Monster, the Yeti...\n"
msgstr ""
"《世界神秘生物百科全书》。\n"
"尼斯湖水怪、雪人……\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/17
msgid ""
"UMAs. Yeah, I know.\n"
msgstr ""
"未知生物。嗯，我知道。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/18
msgid ""
"He's still so much like a boy... I worry about him.\n"
msgstr ""
"他还像个孩子……我很担心他。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/19
msgid ""
"He'll be fine. I know plenty of grown men who still\n"
"go crazy over UMAs.\n"
msgstr ""
"他会没事。我认识不少成年男人，至今\n"
"还为UMA着迷。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/20
msgid ""
"Are... are you serious?\n"
msgstr ""
"你……当真？\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/0
msgid ""
"You've taken such good care of me since you\n"
"saved me from el colibri.\n"
msgstr ""
"你从el colibri手中救了我，\n"
"一直照顾我到现在。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/1
msgid ""
"I want to return the favor.\n"
msgstr ""
"我想报答你。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/2
msgid ""
"Just wait until you're healed up. Then we'll talk.\n"
msgstr ""
"等你伤好了再说。到时候再谈。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/3
msgid ""
"I appreciate that. But you need all the help you\n"
"can get.\n"
msgstr ""
"我很感激。但你需要一切能得到的\n"
"帮助。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/4
msgid ""
"It might take a while for me to heal completely,\n"
msgstr ""
"我完全康复可能要一段时间，\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/5
msgid ""
"but I'll be fine once I'm on my feet. Put me in a\n"
"combat unit - I'll pull my weight.\n"
msgstr ""
"但我能站起来就没事。把我编入\n"
"战斗单位，我会尽本分。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/6
msgid ""
"I wouldn't expect any less from a Sandinista\n"
"comandante.\n"
msgstr ""
"对桑地诺\n"
"指挥官也不会有别的期待。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/7
msgid ""
"Enough flattery.\n"
msgstr ""
"别拍马屁。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/8
msgid ""
"But seriously, it does not feel right for me to be\n"
"sitting here while my compas are out risking their\n"
"lives.\n"
msgstr ""
"但说真的，战友们在外\n"
"拼命，我却坐在这里，\n"
"心里不是滋味。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/9
msgid ""
"One thing's for sure. Having you out in the field\n"
"would be a big boost to Sandinista morale.\n"
msgstr ""
"有一点可以肯定。有你亲临前线，\n"
"会大大鼓舞桑地诺的士气。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/10
msgid ""
"Of course, our ultimate goal is still the overthrow\n"
"of Somoza.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然，我们的最终目标仍然是推翻\n"
"索摩查。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/11
msgid ""
"But until we get ourselves back in order, we will\n"
"follow your lead, wherever it takes us.\n"
msgstr ""
"但在我们重整旗鼓之前，我们会\n"
"追随你的领导，无论去向何方。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/12
msgid ""
"Glad to have you on board.\n"
msgstr ""
"很高兴你加入。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/0
msgid ""
"Amanda, you getting used to Mother Base?\n"
msgstr ""
"阿曼达，在母基地还习惯吗？\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/1
msgid ""
"Yes, it is Heaven compared to living in the\n"
"mountains.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，比起山里，\n"
"这里就是天堂。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/2
msgid ""
"We're no longer constantly on the run from la\n"
"Guardia or mercenaries.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们不再需要时刻躲避国民警卫队\n"
"或雇佣兵了。\n"
